# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# Defense-in-depth only: npm gives the package.json "files" allowlist
# precedence over a root .npmignore, so paths matched by "files" cannot be
# re-excluded here. The authoritative bytecode/cache excludes are the "!"
# negation patterns inside the "files" field itself (verified via
# `npm pack --dry-run`). These lines only take effect if the "files"
# allowlist is ever removed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
